# A `join` condition must be a column name or `$left.a == $right.b` (DS1030).
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime); 'customers.csv'(customerId: string, name: string, country: string, signupDate: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on amount > 1;
from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on customerId == customerId;
from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on $left.customerId == $left.orderId
---- expected
error[DS1030]: a `join` condition must be a column name or `$left.a == $right.b`
  --> query:1:45
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on amount > 1;
  |                                             ^^^^^^^^^^ not a `join` condition
  |
  = help: `join` compares columns: compute `amount > 1` with `extend` on each side first, then name the new column after `on`

error[DS1030]: a `join` condition must be a column name or `$left.a == $right.b`
  --> query:2:45
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on customerId == customerId;
  |                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a `join` condition
  |
  = help: to join on the column both tables have, name it once: `on customerId`

error[DS1030]: both sides of this `join` condition use `$left`
  --> query:3:45
  |
3 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on $left.customerId == $left.orderId
  |                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this compares one table with itself
  |
  = help: compare a left column with a right one: `$left.a == $right.b`

query 1 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
  customerId1: string
  name: string
  country: string
  signupDate: datetime

query 2 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
  customerId1: string
  name: string
  country: string
  signupDate: datetime

query 3 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
  customerId1: string
  name: string
  country: string
  signupDate: datetime
